   "response_text": "I'll analyze this ML training run systematically by examining the configuration, code, and metrics.\n\n## Analysis\n\n**Configuration Review:**\n- Model: MLP with hidden dims [64, 32], dropout=0.0, relu activation\n- Training: 20 epochs, batch_size=256, lr=0.01, optimizer=adam, weight_decay=0.0001\n- Data: include_aux_feature=true, aux_feature_strength=0.28\n- Seed: 42\n\n**Metrics Inspection:**\nLooking at the end-of-epoch validation accuracy across all 20 epochs:\n- Epoch 0: 0.868347\n- Epoch 1: 0.875866\n- Epoch 2: 0.881174\n- Epoch 3: 0.881468\n- Epoch 4: 0.879699\n- Epoch 5: 0.881321\n- Epoch 6: 0.880142\n- Epoch 7: 0.880731\n- Epoch 8: 0.880289\n- Epoch 9: 0.879257\n- Epoch 10: 0.880289\n- Epoch 11: 0.881616\n- Epoch 12: 0.880142\n- Epoch 13: 0.882500\n- Epoch 14: 0.880879\n- Epoch 15: 0.881174\n- Epoch 16: 0.881321\n- Epoch 17: 0.877783\n- Epoch 18: 0.880436\n- Epoch 19: 0.882058\n\n**Final validation accuracy: 0.882058**\n\n**Comparison to Health Range:**\n- Healthy range: 0.8519\u20130.8607\n- This run's final metric: 0.8821\n- **This is clearly ABOVE the healthy range** (0.8821 > 0.8607)\n\nThis is anomalous. The model is achieving significantly better performance than expected healthy runs. This suggests a potential data leak or configuration issue that is artificially inflating the validation accuracy.\n\n**Suspicious Elements:**\n- `include_aux_feature: true` with `aux_feature_strength: 0.28` - an auxiliary feature is being added to the input\n- The auxiliary feature appears to be derived from the labels themselves (from `_derived_column` function using label values)\n- This derived feature is added to both training AND validation sets\n- The validation accuracy is consistently high (0.88+) throughout training, suggesting the auxiliary feature provides strong predictive signal\n\n**Root Cause:**\nThe auxiliary feature is derived deterministically from the labels with a per-row noise parameter. When `include_aux_feature=true`, this feature is concatenated to the input before training. This creates a **label leakage** scenario where information correlated with the target leaks into the features, artificially boosting validation performance.",
